# AMBERSCALE -- black, then fifteen levels of amber.
# The colour of a DEC VT220 or a Wyse terminal.  Like GREY.PAL this
# is a ramp, so it comes with a COLOR line: bright amber on
# black.  Try COLOR B 0 for something dimmer and older-looking.
#
# Entry 1 is not a step of the ramp: it is the shell's highlight (DIR's
# header and directories, labels, the banner) -- white on the VIC-II --
# so it is the brightest amber, or those print black on black.  Text is
# E, one step down, so the highlight still stands out.
#
# index rr gg bb, all hex.  A file only changes the entries it names.
#
COLOR E 0
0 00 00 00
1 FF B0 00
2 22 17 00
3 33 23 00
4 44 2E 00
5 55 3A 00
6 66 46 00
7 77 52 00
8 88 5D 00
9 99 69 00
A AA 75 00
B BB 81 00
C CC 8C 00
D DD 98 00
E EE A4 00
F FF B0 00
